```
public void switchAudioTrack(int index)
    {
        // TrackManager.getInstance().initTrack(mInternalPlayer, index);
        List<MultiTrackAudioRender> trackRenders = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < mInternalPlayer.getRendererCount(); i++)
        {
            if (mInternalPlayer.getRenderer(i).getTrackType() == C.TRACK_TYPE_AUDIO)
            {
                trackRenders.add((MultiTrackAudioRender)mInternalPlayer.getRenderer(i));
            }
        }
        if (trackRenders.size() > 0)
        {
            for (int i = 0; i < trackRenders.size(); i++)
            {
                MultiTrackAudioRender audioRender = trackRenders.get(i);
                if (index == i)
                {
                    audioRender.SetVolume(1.0f);
                }
                else
                {
                    audioRender.SetVolume(0.0f);
                }
            }
        }
    }
```

The core idea is to render multiple audio tracks at the same time,then play one of these tracks and mute others.

